WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:03.190
INTRO:
Not too long ago, Saudi Arabia was a desolate

00:00:03.190 --> 00:00:06.800
wasteland filled with tribes who were fighting
for survival.

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:12.639
The area had extremely low economic activity,
and aside from Mecca, they had nothing going

00:00:12.639 --> 00:00:13.690
for them.

00:00:13.690 --> 00:00:19.210
On March 3, 1938, however, all of this would
change when the Americans found the world’s

00:00:19.210 --> 00:00:22.060
largest petroleum reserves.

00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:26.770
Over the next few decades, much of the profits
from the area went to the Americans while

00:00:26.770 --> 00:00:29.870
Saudi Arabia was left with measly dividends.

00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:35.059
But, Saudi Arabia slowly saved up these dividends
and started buying up these oil companies

00:00:35.059 --> 00:00:37.100
that were drilling across their country.

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:42.449
And eventually, by 1980, the Saudi government
would grow their stake to a 100% which made

00:00:42.449 --> 00:00:47.879
them the owners of the most profitable company
in the world: Saudi Aramco.

00:00:47.879 --> 00:00:52.420
Saudi Aramco has since revolutionized the
area into a modern desert oasis.

00:00:52.420 --> 00:00:58.050
But, while their cities are more modern than
even western cities, they still have one fatal

00:00:58.050 --> 00:01:01.800
bottleneck: 92% of their budget comes from
oil.

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:06.530
Now, most of us have been led to believe that
Saudi Arabia has enough oil to run for several

00:01:06.530 --> 00:01:09.240
decades if not over a century.

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:14.630
But, many experts disagree, because there
is evidence that Saudi Arabia may have been

00:01:14.630 --> 00:01:16.619
lying about their oil reserves.

00:01:16.619 --> 00:01:22.469
So, how much longer till Saudi Arabia really
runs out of oil?

00:01:22.469 --> 00:01:28.780
SKETCHY DATA:
To figure out how much time Saudi Arabia has

00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:33.530
left, we can approach the problem in two different
ways which are the supply approach and the

00:01:33.530 --> 00:01:34.530
demand approach.

00:01:34.530 --> 00:01:38.130
For this video, we’re mainly gonna focus
on the supply.

00:01:38.130 --> 00:01:42.969
Saudi Arabia is estimated to have 260 billion
barrels of oil left.

00:01:42.969 --> 00:01:48.150
And over the past 10 years, Saudi Arabia has
on average pumped out roughly 10 million barrels

00:01:48.150 --> 00:01:49.810
of oil per day.

00:01:49.810 --> 00:01:55.460
This means that over an entire year, Saudi
Arabia pumps out approximately 3.65 billion

00:01:55.460 --> 00:01:56.500
barrels of oil.

00:01:56.500 --> 00:02:00.680
Doing some simple math, we’d find out that
if Saudi Arabia maintains their current output,

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:06.090
they’d run out of oil in 71.2 years or sometime
in the mid 2090s.

00:02:06.090 --> 00:02:10.890
This might sound like a long time away, but
the thing to keep in mind is that it’s already

00:02:10.890 --> 00:02:15.069
been 84 years since Saudi Arabia started pulling
in oil revenue.

00:02:15.069 --> 00:02:19.870
This means that Saudi Arabia is over half
way through their oil roller coaster.

00:02:19.870 --> 00:02:22.989
But, things may be a lot worse than this.

00:02:22.989 --> 00:02:29.150
You see, a lot of experts think that Saudi
Arabia has been lying about their oil reserves.

00:02:29.150 --> 00:02:33.590
All of the oil reserve estimates that we’ve
gotten for decades now is from Saudi Arabia

00:02:33.590 --> 00:02:37.230
themselves and the data is rather sketchy.

00:02:37.230 --> 00:02:43.120
First of all, in 1989, Saudi Arabia’s oil
reserves just randomly skyrocketed from 170

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:45.150
billion to 260 billion.

00:02:45.150 --> 00:02:50.790
But, all of Saudi’s biggest oil fields were
discovered between 1936 and 1970.

00:02:50.790 --> 00:02:56.040
And no comparable discoveries have been made
in the last 50 years, so how did their reserves

00:02:56.040 --> 00:02:59.870
apparently jump by 90 billion barrels overnight.

00:02:59.870 --> 00:03:04.379
Something else to note is that the timing
of this jump was also super sketchy.

00:03:04.379 --> 00:03:09.620
While Saudi Arabia took control of Aramco
in 1980, it wasn’t until 1988 that the Americans

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:13.470
were fully pushed out and Saudi leadership
was established.

00:03:13.470 --> 00:03:18.250
And somehow, just one year after this change
in leadership, their oil reserves skyrocketed

00:03:18.250 --> 00:03:19.250
by 50%.

00:03:19.250 --> 00:03:22.770
Now, that’s definitely quite suspicious.

00:03:22.770 --> 00:03:28.220
Also, Saudi Arabia has been claiming that
their oil reserves haven’t changed in 33

00:03:28.220 --> 00:03:29.220
years.

00:03:29.220 --> 00:03:33.049
This doesn’t seem all that likely given
how much oil they’ve pumped out in the past

00:03:33.049 --> 00:03:34.489
33 years.

00:03:34.489 --> 00:03:38.360
Going back to the Saudi oil output graph,
we can see that Saudi Arabia has averaged

00:03:38.360 --> 00:03:42.500
about 8.5 million barrels of oil over past
3 decades.

00:03:42.500 --> 00:03:46.930
This works out to a total output of 102 billion
barrels of oil.

00:03:46.930 --> 00:03:51.730
Also, if we look more closely at the Saudi’s
reserve data, we’ll see that they have not

00:03:51.730 --> 00:03:55.530
only been claiming that their oil reserves
have stayed constant, but they’ve actually

00:03:55.530 --> 00:03:57.490
been claiming that it’s been increasing.

00:03:57.490 --> 00:04:04.950
In 1990, there were 258 billion barrels of
oil but as of 2016, there were 266 billion

00:04:04.950 --> 00:04:06.200
barrels of oil.

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:10.819
This means that Saudi Arabia was not only
able to pump out 102 billion barrels over

00:04:10.819 --> 00:04:16.600
the last 30 years, but they were able to come
out on top by 8 billion barrels.

00:04:16.600 --> 00:04:21.699
In other words, Saudi Arabia has been able
to find a 110 billion barrels since the Americans

00:04:21.699 --> 00:04:22.699
left.

00:04:22.699 --> 00:04:26.810
And that’s in addition to the initial 90
billion barrel jump.

00:04:26.810 --> 00:04:31.750
So, apparently, Saudi Arabia has found a total
of 200 billion barrels of oil since they took

00:04:31.750 --> 00:04:32.750
over.

00:04:32.750 --> 00:04:36.850
Keep in mind, this figure is 30 billion barrels
more than what the Americans estimated Saudi

00:04:36.850 --> 00:04:38.940
Arabia had in total in the 1980s.

00:04:38.940 --> 00:04:43.880
Now, I know a lot of people aren’t exactly
fans of Americans.

00:04:43.880 --> 00:04:48.850
But, one thing I think we can all agree about
is that Americans are phenomenal at capitalistic

00:04:48.850 --> 00:04:49.850
exploitation.

00:04:49.850 --> 00:04:55.440
So, the idea that the Americas exploited Saudi
Arabia for 50 years and didn’t even find

00:04:55.440 --> 00:05:00.880
half of their oil reserves (AKA 200 billion
barrels) seems pretty far fetched to me, but

00:05:00.880 --> 00:05:03.380
I’ll let you be the judge of that.

00:05:03.380 --> 00:05:09.090
WHY LIE:
It’s not just the data that’s pointing

00:05:09.090 --> 00:05:10.650
to inconsistencies either.

00:05:10.650 --> 00:05:14.470
There have been some major leaks over the
years that have pointed towards the Saudis

00:05:14.470 --> 00:05:15.470
lying.

00:05:15.470 --> 00:05:20.370
In 2011 for example, we saw a leak from WikiLeaks
that claimed to cover insider info from a

00:05:20.370 --> 00:05:22.060
high level Saudi oil executive.

00:05:22.060 --> 00:05:26.700
According to the executive, over the years,
Saudi Arabia had been overstating their oil

00:05:26.700 --> 00:05:30.070
reserves by as much as 300 billion barrels.

00:05:30.070 --> 00:05:35.440
Also, something else to note is that Saudi
Arabia has never been able to pump up production

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:36.820
that much.

00:05:36.820 --> 00:05:41.130
If they truly found another 200 billion, you
would think they would have plenty of new

00:05:41.130 --> 00:05:43.500
oil fields to drill from and increase production.

00:05:43.500 --> 00:05:46.940
Yet, they have been unable to top what the
Americans got them to.

00:05:46.940 --> 00:05:50.370
You see, 10 million barrels per day is nothing
new.

00:05:50.370 --> 00:05:55.270
In fact, the Americans were able to reach
this level with Saudi Arabia way back in 1980

00:05:55.270 --> 00:05:57.750
when they reached 9.9 million barrels per
day.

00:05:57.750 --> 00:06:03.910
It’s been 42 years since then, but the Saudi’s
have barely been able to reach 10.7 million

00:06:03.910 --> 00:06:05.009
barrels per day.

00:06:05.009 --> 00:06:09.069
Also, it doesn’t seem like the Saudis are
holding back either.

00:06:09.069 --> 00:06:13.810
For example, even with Donald Trump threatened
to withdraw military support, Saudi Arabia

00:06:13.810 --> 00:06:17.610
couldn’t increase production to over 10.5
million barrels per day.

00:06:17.610 --> 00:06:22.289
Now, you could say that Saudi Arabia refused
to respond to threats, but they weren’t

00:06:22.289 --> 00:06:26.490
able to increase production even when they
were the ones that were issuing the threat.

00:06:26.490 --> 00:06:31.310
For example, remember when oil prices crashed
between 2014 and 2016.

00:06:31.310 --> 00:06:36.990
Oil prices crashed from $120 to just $42 and
one of the main reasons for this was Saudi

00:06:36.990 --> 00:06:37.990
Arabia.

00:06:37.990 --> 00:06:42.870
You see, the US was making strides when it
came to extracting oil from oil shales.

00:06:42.870 --> 00:06:46.430
This meant that the US would become less dependent
on the middle east for oil.

00:06:46.430 --> 00:06:51.699
So, Saudi Arabia and OPEC decided to launch
a price war against shale oil extracters.

00:06:51.699 --> 00:06:55.990
The idea was to pump up oil production and
crash oil prices to run these extracters out

00:06:55.990 --> 00:06:57.280
of business.

00:06:57.280 --> 00:07:01.259
This would’ve been the perfect time for
Saudi Arabia to pump up production to 15 or

00:07:01.259 --> 00:07:09.069
even 20 million barrels per day, but they
weren’t even able to cross 11 million barrels.

00:07:09.069 --> 00:07:15.879
Clearly, Saudi Arabia can’t even surpass
the ceiling that the Americans got them to

00:07:15.879 --> 00:07:19.470
which just makes it even more likely that
they’ve been lying about reserves.

00:07:19.470 --> 00:07:22.879
But, all of this brings up the question, why
lie?

00:07:22.879 --> 00:07:26.690
Wouldn’t it be better for Saudi Arabia if
everyone knew that oil reserves weren’t

00:07:26.690 --> 00:07:27.690
as plentiful.

00:07:27.690 --> 00:07:32.240
Less supply equals higher prices which means
more profit for Saudi Arabia right?

00:07:32.240 --> 00:07:36.850
Well, this would be true at the beginning,
but it wouldn’t last long.

00:07:36.850 --> 00:07:41.470
You see, even with Saudi Arabia’s likely
inflated figures, they don’t actually hold

00:07:41.470 --> 00:07:43.370
the world’s largest oil reserve.

00:07:43.370 --> 00:07:47.270
This title actually goes to Venezuela who
holds 300 billion barrels.

00:07:47.270 --> 00:07:51.740
Now, Venezuela oil has never been that helpful
to the world because the country has been

00:07:51.740 --> 00:07:55.699
plagued with corruption, hyperinflation, and
who knows what else.

00:07:55.699 --> 00:07:59.940
But, the second the world knows for sure that
Saudi Arabia doesn’t have as much as they

00:07:59.940 --> 00:08:03.300
said, they’re gonna turn their entire focus
onto the remaining countries.

00:08:03.300 --> 00:08:06.430
We’ll see historic strides in Venezuela
and Canada.

00:08:06.430 --> 00:08:09.860
Heck, we might even see the western world
make amends with Russia.

00:08:09.860 --> 00:08:15.830
At the same time, the push for renewable energy
will also become stronger than ever before,

00:08:15.830 --> 00:08:19.639
and all of this will reduce the world’s
dependency on Saudi Arabia.

00:08:19.639 --> 00:08:24.050
And given that oil is the only thing that
gives Saudi Arabia any sort of significance

00:08:24.050 --> 00:08:28.710
on the world economic stage, this would not
be in Saudi Arabia’s best interest.

00:08:28.710 --> 00:08:32.590
For them, it’s best to keep the rest of
the world as dependent as possible on their

00:08:32.590 --> 00:08:33.650
oil.

00:08:33.650 --> 00:08:37.700
And if that means lying about their oil reserves,
then so be it.

00:08:37.700 --> 00:08:42.910
THE COUNTDOWN:
But, if Saudi Arabia has been lying about

00:08:42.910 --> 00:08:47.780
their reserves this entire time, how much
time do we actually have until they run out?

00:08:47.780 --> 00:08:52.260
Well, if we assume that the last accurate
piece of data we have is from 1988 when the

00:08:52.260 --> 00:08:57.510
Americans left, this means that Saudi Arabia
was left with a 170 billion barrels of oil.

00:08:57.510 --> 00:09:02.570
Realistically, it’s possible that they’ve
increased this amount by 10-20% over the past

00:09:02.570 --> 00:09:07.270
34 years, so we’ll give them the benefit
of the doubt and call it 200 billion barrels.

00:09:07.270 --> 00:09:12.630
At 8.5 million barrels per day on average,
Saudi Arabia would have used up 105 billion

00:09:12.630 --> 00:09:14.350
barrels since 1988.

00:09:14.350 --> 00:09:17.560
This would levae them with 95 billion barrels
left today.

00:09:17.560 --> 00:09:21.480
If Saudi Arabia continues to average 8 to
10 million barrels per day, this would mean

00:09:21.480 --> 00:09:24.820
that they only have roughly 25 to 30 years
left.

00:09:24.820 --> 00:09:29.520
If Saudi Arabia has been lying, then I think
this is likely a pretty realistic estimate.

00:09:29.520 --> 00:09:34.730
Now, we could of course go full tin foil hat
mode and become doomsday theoriziers.

00:09:34.730 --> 00:09:39.830
What if Saudi Arabia found no new oil after
the Americans left and what if 20% of the

00:09:39.830 --> 00:09:43.060
remaining 170 billion was unusable?

00:09:43.060 --> 00:09:48.360
This would mean that Saudi Arabia only had
136 billion barrels of usable oil in 1988.

00:09:48.360 --> 00:09:52.740
Given that we’ve used approximately 105
billion over the past 34 years, this would

00:09:52.740 --> 00:09:54.730
leave them with just 31 billion barrels today.

00:09:54.730 --> 00:09:58.850
And at this rate, they’d be out in just
10 years.

00:09:58.850 --> 00:10:02.340
While that sounds scary, it’s more than
likely not true.

00:10:02.340 --> 00:10:06.580
While Saudi Arabia may be lying about having
70 to 100 years worth of oil left, it’s

00:10:06.580 --> 00:10:09.080
likely that they atleast have a few decades
left.

00:10:09.080 --> 00:10:12.290
And this matches up with the kingdom’s actions
as well.

00:10:12.290 --> 00:10:16.030
If they truly had several decades worth of
oil left, I don’t think they’d be going

00:10:16.030 --> 00:10:18.330
all in on growing other sources of revenue.

00:10:18.330 --> 00:10:22.860
Over the past couple of years, Saudi Arabia
has made insane strides when it comes to adopting

00:10:22.860 --> 00:10:23.860
western standards.

00:10:23.860 --> 00:10:29.360
Women’s rights and human rights have gotten
significantly better, and they’ve even opened

00:10:29.360 --> 00:10:31.820
up the country to tourism for the first time.

00:10:31.820 --> 00:10:36.041
They’ve also been pouring billions of dollars
into airports and tourist attractions, so

00:10:36.041 --> 00:10:39.690
it’s seems like they’re pretty determined
to turn the country into a tourist hub just

00:10:39.690 --> 00:10:40.690
like Dubai.

00:10:40.690 --> 00:10:45.620
There’s also the whole Vision 2030 project
led by Mohammed Bin Salman which aims to significantly

00:10:45.620 --> 00:10:48.240
reduce the country’s dependence on oil.

00:10:48.240 --> 00:10:52.440
If such projects go well, I think it’s pretty
realistic for Saudi Arabia to become independent

00:10:52.440 --> 00:10:54.810
from oil by the time they run dry.

00:10:54.810 --> 00:10:58.740
So, while they may be tricking the entire
world regarding their reserves, they’re

00:10:58.740 --> 00:11:03.400
not tricking themselves, and they’re getting
prepared for a future without oil.

00:11:03.400 --> 00:11:09.240
THE FUTURE OF SAUDI ARABIA:
While we can argue that lying about their

00:11:09.240 --> 00:11:14.300
reserves is unethical and manipulative, from
an objective perspective, they’ve actually

00:11:14.300 --> 00:11:16.210
played their cards really well.

00:11:16.210 --> 00:11:20.050
By overstating their reserves, they’ve been
able to maintain their dominance wihtin oil

00:11:20.050 --> 00:11:21.180
industry.

00:11:21.180 --> 00:11:25.020
Their crude oil exports are literally twice
as high as second place.

00:11:25.020 --> 00:11:29.800
This has allowed them build up a war chest
that’s worth nearly half a trillion dollars.

00:11:29.800 --> 00:11:35.570
They also took Saudi Aramco public a few years
ago at a $2 trillion valuation, so it looks

00:11:35.570 --> 00:11:38.900
like they’re slowly wanting to cash out
over there as well.

00:11:38.900 --> 00:11:43.350
In the meantime, they’ve also started to
aggressively diversify their income streams,

00:11:43.350 --> 00:11:48.380
so it looks like Saudi Arabia is poised do
extremely well even after the run out of oil.

00:11:48.380 --> 00:11:53.460
As for the rest of us, we may not have as
much oil left as we originally thought, but

00:11:53.460 --> 00:11:55.700
maybe that’s a good thing.

00:11:55.700 --> 00:12:00.390
Maybe this is exactly we need to finally make
the jump to renewable forms of energy and

00:12:00.390 --> 00:12:04.520
leave our gas guzzling days in the past, but
that’s just what I think.

00:12:04.520 --> 00:12:07.550
Do you think Saudi Arabia’s oil reserves
are sketch?

00:12:07.550 --> 00:12:09.100
Comment that down below.

00:12:09.100 --> 00:12:12.330
Also, drop a like if you’re excited for
a renewable future.

